// # Ooda Build Cluster — Anchor for Agents
//
// Logline: Front door for the build/, deliver/, and introspect/ command surface. The largest subdir; it groups the build-toolchain drivers with the project-init and code-generation utilities.
//
// Setup: The build/ cluster has 8 sub-files. The args/find_compiler/host_run/host_build/json_check/reproducible/ files drive oodac. The context/health/test/install/gen/bench/init files are the user-facing project commands.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Toolchain plumbing: args, find_compiler, host_run, host_build, json_check, reproducible — all spawn oodac.
//   2. Build-time diagnostics: context, health — read the project tree under FsReadCap.
//   3. Code generation: gen — scaffold a new .oo file from a template.
//   4. Project lifecycle: init (bootstrap a project), test (compile and run one .oo test), install (install a pre-built pack), bench (time oodac check/run).

import "args.oo";
import "find_compiler.oo";
import "host_run.oo";
import "host_build.oo";
import "json_check.oo";
import "reproducible.oo";
import "context.oo";
import "health.oo";
import "test.oo";
import "install.oo";
import "gen.oo";
import "bench.oo";
import "init.oo";
